# The repo publishes the site and what a developer needs to work on it.
# Everything below is studio-side: the brief, brand doc and wireframes, the
# event-site reference build, the QA harness, the AI portrait working files,
# and assets the site never loads. The four technical docs are kept: the
# design system, motion, responsive rules and code conventions (14 Oct, for
# the handover to TEKEX's developer).
.claude/
CLAUDE.md
PROMPT.md
docs/*
!docs/02-design-system.md
!docs/03-motion.md
!docs/04-responsive.md
!docs/05-conventions.md
reference/
qa/
output/
assets/reference/
assets/social-templates/
assets/speakers/
assets/event-subbrand/
# videos from the event site that this site doesn't serve (~37 MB);
# banner-loop.mp4 is a source for build/asset-scripts/films/edit_reels.py
assets/video/banner-loop.mp4
assets/video/closing-loop*
assets/video/footer-loop.mp4
assets/video/hero-loop*
assets/video/overview-4-5*

# Source films (owner's edits and the brand films, 75-335MB each). The site
# serves the short cuts made from them (assets/video/hero-reel-*, loop-reel-*):
# see build/asset-scripts/films/edit_reels.py.
Video assets/
# event poster originals (downloaded from the URLs in build/asset-scripts/events/originals.json)
build/asset-scripts/events/orig/

# Event photography originals (full-resolution, 8-16MB each). The site uses
# web-sized copies made from them in assets/photography/.
Photo assets/
